  "question": {
    "text": "The mass per unit length of a uniform wire is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>135</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. A transverse wave of the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>21</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is produced in it, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is in meter and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is in second. Then, the expected value of tension in the wire is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>. Value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is <u>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</u>&nbsp;(Round-off to the nearest integer)"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "1215",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>135</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>gm</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0135</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>21</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> in meter &amp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> in sec)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>30</mn><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>T</mi><mi>&#956;</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>30</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0135</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>15</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1215</mn></math></p>"
